# Per-environment tfvars are RENDERED from the LandingZone spec
# (environments/<env>.yaml is the source of truth) by `llz render`, and
# regenerated in CI before every terraform op (the terraform-init composite runs
# `llz render --tfvars-only`). They are transient build artifacts — NOT committed
# — so a spec edit produces one reviewable diff (the spec) instead of two, and a
# rendered-but-unformatted tfvars can never trip the pre-commit `tofu fmt -check`.
#
# Matches cluster/<env>.tfvars, object-storage/<env>.tfvars,
# databases/<env>.tfvars, and vpc/<network>.tfvars. The committed
# terraform.tfvars.example defaults stay tracked (they end in .example, not
# .tfvars). A working `llz` is therefore required for any terraform op — see
# docs/landing-zone-spec.md.
#
# Legacy (pre-spec) instances never run `llz render`, so they never receive this
# file; their hand-authored <env>.tfvars stay tracked as the source of truth.
*/*.tfvars

# The TF roots' *.tf (cluster, object-storage, databases, vpc) are generated on the fly by `llz render` from the
# embedded tfroots package (like the per-env *.tfvars) — an instance commits ZERO
# Terraform code, only the .terraform.lock.hcl provider pins. See tools/internal/shared/tfroots.
*/*.tf

# The provider lockfile is generated too, and for the same reason the *.tf above
# are: the pin and the `required_providers` constraint it has to satisfy are two
# halves of one decision, and they now travel together inside the llz binary
# (tools/internal/shared/tfroots/roots/<root>/) instead of one shipping in the ci
# image and the other sitting committed here.
#
# THE SPLIT THIS ENDS. The lock used to be `owned` in .template-manifest — seeded
# at scaffold time and never re-touched by an upgrade — while the constraint moved
# with each release. So a release that raised one left EVERY instance in the field
# pinned below it, hard-blocked at the first step of every terraform op:
#
#   locked provider registry.opentofu.org/linode/linode 3.12.0 does not match
#   configured version constraint ~> 4.3
#
# while a fresh scaffold and release-e2e (which force-pushes a new instantiation
# every run) both stayed green. Greenfield passed, brownfield broke, and no lane
# could see the difference. Rendering it removes the state rather than checking it.
#
# Legacy (pre-spec) instances never run `llz render`, so they never receive this
# file; whatever lock they committed stays theirs, next to the *.tf they also own.
*/.terraform.lock.hcl
